WEBVTT

00:00:09.500 --> 00:00:13.160
A species on the brink of extinction, the twintail mermaid...

00:00:13.870 --> 00:00:15.230
Attention:

00:00:15.580 --> 00:00:17.360
Do not tell a lie.

00:00:18.250 --> 00:00:21.860
This species can tell when a person is lying.

00:00:26.360 --> 00:00:28.400
She can tell when I lie? Ha!

00:00:30.740 --> 00:00:32.290
I paid a pretty penny for you!

00:00:32.850 --> 00:00:35.880
I'll take <i>real</i> good care of you...

00:00:37.670 --> 00:00:40.380
Now, come on out...

00:00:46.950 --> 00:00:49.520
That's a good girl! I won't hurt you, I promise!

00:00:57.280 --> 00:01:01.070
Right now, hundreds of different alien species are coming and going from the Earth.

00:01:02.200 --> 00:01:05.450
Species that come in peace. Aggressive, warlike species...

00:01:05.450 --> 00:01:07.530
Species on the brink of extinction...

00:01:08.530 --> 00:01:11.410
All manner of different species live here,

00:01:11.540 --> 00:01:15.960
each with their own purpose, such as research, intrigue, or profit...

00:01:18.600 --> 00:01:19.650
Liar.

00:01:25.230 --> 00:01:29.470
The towns entrance is adorned with a cow's skull

00:01:30.420 --> 00:01:34.210
It's fine that the law is decided by the strongest,

00:01:35.630 --> 00:01:39.390
But this simple feeling will not be enough to fulfill you

00:01:40.620 --> 00:01:45.070
Everyone will definitely revolt and shortly disappear

00:01:45.190 --> 00:01:50.160
That's a shocking bloody picture

00:01:50.160 --> 00:01:55.500
I'm feeling nauseous

00:01:55.500 --> 00:02:05.880
Holding my head, I board the subway

00:02:05.880 --> 00:02:16.060
Righteous way of living, righteous way of dying

00:02:16.060 --> 00:02:26.360
Who on earth knows or what the hell can show me?

00:02:33.820 --> 00:02:36.870
Cold finger girl

00:02:44.170 --> 00:02:45.990
Sit Down

00:02:57.800 --> 00:03:02.080
We only got a little bit longer before all that money we promised her.

00:03:02.080 --> 00:03:03.690
What are we gonna do then?

00:03:06.330 --> 00:03:09.550
The last mermaid... She made us plenty.

00:03:10.100 --> 00:03:12.740
After she keeps her promise, then...

00:03:13.090 --> 00:03:16.620
I'd say, stuffing her, or selling her scales will do.

00:03:17.580 --> 00:03:18.240
You think?

00:03:23.650 --> 00:03:25.120
Here she comes.

00:03:30.350 --> 00:03:33.560
That was fast. You killed him as well?

00:03:33.560 --> 00:03:36.060
Yeah. This planet's full of liars.

00:03:36.060 --> 00:03:38.340
But it makes us plenty of cash.

00:03:38.340 --> 00:03:39.010
Let's go.

00:03:39.180 --> 00:03:40.600
The next customer awaits.

00:03:50.870 --> 00:03:52.220
I'm off!

00:03:52.220 --> 00:03:53.730
Okay, I'm leaving!

00:03:53.730 --> 00:03:55.690
Right, have a nice day!

00:03:58.380 --> 00:04:00.770
Now then... Just a few more, and then we're done.

00:04:01.920 --> 00:04:07.860
Due to his father's work, Shimizu Yoshiki-kun will be moving to America.

00:04:18.650 --> 00:04:19.640
When are you leaving?

00:04:20.030 --> 00:04:20.740
Day after tomorrow.

00:04:20.740 --> 00:04:22.770
What?! So soon?

00:04:22.770 --> 00:04:26.620
If your dad's being transferred, why doesn't he just go himself?

00:04:26.620 --> 00:04:29.890
Mom's dead-set against the family living apart.

00:04:30.430 --> 00:04:32.110
Then why don't you stay behind yourself?

00:04:32.110 --> 00:04:33.650
You can live at my place.

00:04:35.750 --> 00:04:37.990
I can't ask to live with you for five years.

00:04:40.320 --> 00:04:43.060
What about the karate tournament this summer?

00:04:43.060 --> 00:04:44.210
Not gonna let me have my rematch?

00:04:44.720 --> 00:04:48.500
I'd say something like, "I'll see you at the International Tournament."

00:04:48.800 --> 00:04:52.460
But I was planning on quitting karate when I entered middle school anyway!

00:04:52.740 --> 00:04:53.850
You big liar.

00:04:53.850 --> 00:04:55.190
Seriously, man.

00:04:55.190 --> 00:04:57.450
This isn't the time to be fooling around!

00:04:58.170 --> 00:04:59.720
I ain't fooling around.

00:04:59.720 --> 00:05:00.830
Stop lying!

00:05:00.830 --> 00:05:02.060
I can tell just by looking at your face!

00:05:02.060 --> 00:05:07.070
That's right! Why didn't you tell us earlier about you moving?

00:05:07.520 --> 00:05:08.420
Shut the hell up!

00:05:08.420 --> 00:05:10.970
Why do I have to tell you ass-wipes about every little thing, huh?

00:05:10.970 --> 00:05:12.360
What'd you just call us, huh?

00:05:12.360 --> 00:05:13.280
Oh, you're gonna get it now!

00:05:16.990 --> 00:05:18.130
Enough.

00:05:37.000 --> 00:05:38.260
You sure about that?

00:05:41.370 --> 00:05:45.510
I'm fine. I'll be alone in America anyway.

00:06:13.380 --> 00:06:14.630
Hello.

00:06:18.230 --> 00:06:19.350
Wait right there! I'll go get...

00:06:19.350 --> 00:06:21.680
No! Don't call a doctor or an ambulance!

00:06:22.030 --> 00:06:25.220
I'm... an alien.

00:06:25.460 --> 00:06:26.580
Oh, I see.

00:06:26.580 --> 00:06:28.490
Guess it'd be bad if you were found out.

00:06:28.490 --> 00:06:30.170
What'll I do?

00:06:30.970 --> 00:06:32.320
You're sure straight-laced.

00:06:32.320 --> 00:06:33.780
Be a little surprised, would you?

00:06:34.670 --> 00:06:36.290
I know a lot of aliens, actually.

00:06:36.850 --> 00:06:38.150
My teacher's one, too.

00:06:42.150 --> 00:06:43.700
You're telling the truth.

00:06:43.700 --> 00:06:44.760
You can tell?

00:06:44.760 --> 00:06:49.870
When someone lies to me, my tongue reacts by extending out and attacking.

00:06:51.220 --> 00:06:52.570
R-Really?

00:06:53.200 --> 00:06:55.990
I know! I have a friend who can heal wounds!

00:06:56.780 --> 00:06:57.560
Wait here!

00:07:02.780 --> 00:07:03.750
What's the matter?

00:07:04.250 --> 00:07:06.350
We got in a fight.

00:07:06.920 --> 00:07:09.730
Hurry up and apologize.

00:07:10.280 --> 00:07:11.810
But, it was just before...

00:07:11.810 --> 00:07:12.440
Just go!

00:07:18.400 --> 00:07:21.430
I know what it's like to have someone you want to see, but can't.

00:07:22.280 --> 00:07:24.280
So, don't leave any regrets.

00:07:28.550 --> 00:07:29.490
Sorry, I said too much.

00:07:31.530 --> 00:07:32.280
No, it's fine.

00:07:33.030 --> 00:07:34.250
Thanks. Wait here.

00:08:21.240 --> 00:08:22.240
Shimizu?

00:08:22.970 --> 00:08:26.110
I was wrong! I shouldn't have kept from you that I was moving!

00:08:27.210 --> 00:08:29.790
Uh... I also went too far.

00:08:29.790 --> 00:08:32.010
I-It was all just so sudden.

00:08:32.280 --> 00:08:33.520
Yokota, I'm sorry!

00:08:35.660 --> 00:08:37.430
Enough already.

00:08:37.430 --> 00:08:40.700
I mean, what are you gonna do? It's your parents' fault anyway.

00:08:41.490 --> 00:08:42.730
Yokota...

00:08:43.070 --> 00:08:44.430
Leave him.

00:08:44.430 --> 00:08:47.280
Shimizu, you came all the way back here to apologize?

00:08:47.760 --> 00:08:50.070
Oh, right! I need your help!

00:09:07.930 --> 00:09:09.680
But I told her to wait...

00:09:09.890 --> 00:09:11.460
That's a lot of blood.

00:09:11.460 --> 00:09:13.900
We have to find her or she might die!

00:09:13.900 --> 00:09:15.280
Let's split up and search.

00:09:15.280 --> 00:09:15.950
Yokota, you too!

00:09:15.950 --> 00:09:16.560
Shimizu.

00:09:17.650 --> 00:09:18.630
What?

00:09:19.060 --> 00:09:21.060
I ain't forgiven you yet, got it?

00:09:21.060 --> 00:09:22.920
Lay off it, man!

00:09:22.920 --> 00:09:25.050
This isn't the time, damn it!

00:09:25.050 --> 00:09:26.940
No, this is the perfect time.

00:09:26.940 --> 00:09:28.580
I won't go along with that.

00:09:28.580 --> 00:09:30.070
Yokota, you bastard!

00:09:30.270 --> 00:09:33.090
Yokota, what do you want me to do?

00:09:33.090 --> 00:09:34.550
Don't ask me.

00:09:34.550 --> 00:09:38.310
"If I told you, it'd just trouble you more," is what he means.

00:09:38.680 --> 00:09:40.420
Mayuzumi, I'm gonna kick your ass.

00:09:40.820 --> 00:09:41.590
Say again?

00:09:41.590 --> 00:09:43.670
Come 'ere, you!

00:09:48.650 --> 00:09:51.500
Stop it!

00:09:56.960 --> 00:09:58.890
That's enough, all of you!

00:09:58.890 --> 00:10:02.660
We're not gonna be together much longer, so why can't we at least get along in the end?!

00:10:02.660 --> 00:10:04.600
You're okay with splitting up on a sour note, huh?!

00:10:04.890 --> 00:10:07.200
Well, I'm not!

00:10:12.690 --> 00:10:14.920
If you fight any more...

00:10:15.900 --> 00:10:20.120
I don't know... what I might do.

00:10:22.210 --> 00:10:24.360
Right, okay then!

00:10:24.360 --> 00:10:27.700
Since Akagawa-kun's started to cry, let's stop the bickering, 'kay?

00:10:28.350 --> 00:10:30.550
Mayuzumi, Yokota, Shimizu... Cease-fire for now.

00:10:30.900 --> 00:10:31.690
Got it?

00:10:31.690 --> 00:10:33.510
No objections.

00:10:33.910 --> 00:10:36.960
Okay, so let's hurry and search for that woman.

00:10:36.960 --> 00:10:38.830
She's injured, so if she isn't treated...

00:10:38.830 --> 00:10:39.210
Right.

00:10:40.140 --> 00:10:42.590
She didn't seem like a bad person, right?

00:10:42.590 --> 00:10:43.550
Yeah.

00:10:43.550 --> 00:10:46.300
She scolded me when I told her I had a fight with my friends.

00:10:46.300 --> 00:10:48.060
She told me to go apologize right away.

00:10:50.350 --> 00:10:53.950
But, she seemed really sad...

00:10:55.440 --> 00:10:56.990
Totally my type.

00:11:07.470 --> 00:11:08.950
Hey!

00:11:09.870 --> 00:11:11.110
Look there.

00:11:11.110 --> 00:11:13.100
It continues over that way.

00:11:26.250 --> 00:11:27.270
Blue Charge!

00:11:27.270 --> 00:11:28.080
Yellow Charge!

00:11:28.080 --> 00:11:28.970
Red Charge!

00:11:28.970 --> 00:11:29.900
White Charge!

00:11:29.900 --> 00:11:31.120
Black Charge.

00:11:32.860 --> 00:11:35.850
Chromatic Squadron, Color Rangers!

00:11:45.540 --> 00:11:46.800
Did you kill her?

00:11:47.810 --> 00:11:50.310
No, I missed her vital organs.

00:11:50.310 --> 00:11:55.040
If she won't return to her mermaid form, she ain't even worth stuffing.

00:11:56.310 --> 00:11:58.310
Hey, bring a mask.

00:11:58.310 --> 00:12:00.740
Just in case, we'll gag the bitch.

00:12:05.620 --> 00:12:07.600
Some Earth brats, huh?

00:12:08.470 --> 00:12:10.680
If you're gonna play warriors of
justice, do it somewhere else.

00:12:11.670 --> 00:12:14.180
If you don't, I'll shoot.

00:12:15.110 --> 00:12:16.240
You guys are...

00:12:16.240 --> 00:12:17.900
You should be fine now.

00:12:21.420 --> 00:12:24.540
You promised! Did you lie to me?

00:12:24.540 --> 00:12:26.570
We didn't lie.

00:12:26.570 --> 00:12:30.370
If we had, we'd be dead after your tongue stabbed into our brains.

00:12:30.720 --> 00:12:31.950
Isn't that right?

00:12:33.060 --> 00:12:34.190
Friends of yours?

00:12:34.190 --> 00:12:35.550
Hardly.

00:12:35.550 --> 00:12:38.570
They're from the same planet as me, but are a different species.

00:12:38.570 --> 00:12:43.020
They're poachers who make money selling off other living creatures.

00:12:43.020 --> 00:12:43.960
I'm...

00:12:44.060 --> 00:12:45.420
their merchandise.

00:12:46.160 --> 00:12:46.840
That's right.

00:12:47.290 --> 00:12:49.940
When we started this business,

00:12:49.940 --> 00:12:54.190
your species had already been devastated by poachers from other planets.

00:12:54.190 --> 00:12:57.230
When we finally found the mermaids,

00:12:57.310 --> 00:12:58.540
all that were left were 5 little kids.

00:13:01.580 --> 00:13:04.400
All we wanted was to live in peace.

00:13:05.540 --> 00:13:07.150
I remember quite well.

00:13:07.810 --> 00:13:10.450
Back then, this is what I said.

00:13:10.450 --> 00:13:13.830
"Even if it's a kid, if you keep it right, it can get 50 customers."

00:13:14.240 --> 00:13:15.350
They're the worst...

00:13:15.350 --> 00:13:16.690
Yeah, worse than you.

00:13:17.070 --> 00:13:20.690
Then one of the brats said this.

00:13:21.080 --> 00:13:26.210
"If you leave the other four be, I'll earn way more than they can for you!"

00:13:27.550 --> 00:13:29.470
It was the same thing my mother said.

00:13:29.790 --> 00:13:33.830
I went crazy back then, and promised without thinking.

00:13:34.640 --> 00:13:35.390
"Fine!"

00:13:36.140 --> 00:13:39.860
"When you're done with the customers, I'll let you go back."

00:13:40.540 --> 00:13:42.400
I was serious back then.

00:13:42.670 --> 00:13:46.310
Really, the greedy are such sinners...

00:13:50.280 --> 00:13:53.470
It'll take money for us to return to the Planet Holn.

00:13:53.470 --> 00:13:55.880
For us it's an abandoned homeland.

00:13:55.880 --> 00:13:57.990
When I thought we'd be going back just for you,

00:13:57.990 --> 00:14:00.120
I suddenly thought, "What a waste!"

00:14:00.590 --> 00:14:02.210
and accidentally shot you.

00:14:05.750 --> 00:14:06.710
Will you forgive me?

00:14:08.030 --> 00:14:09.440
An accident?

00:14:09.440 --> 00:14:11.970
You can't earn anything from killing her, can you?

00:14:12.300 --> 00:14:13.780
I was being impulsive.

00:14:13.780 --> 00:14:14.840
Enough!

00:14:14.840 --> 00:14:18.530
Please, stop acting so foolish. Let's return to your friends.

00:14:24.670 --> 00:14:26.320
He's lying! Don't be fooled!

00:14:26.700 --> 00:14:27.710
But he's not lying.

00:14:27.710 --> 00:14:29.510
Can't you tell how bogus this sounds?

00:14:29.510 --> 00:14:31.140
I know when I hear lies.

00:14:31.870 --> 00:14:33.000
That's right.

00:14:33.000 --> 00:14:37.700
You know all too well that what I say isn't a lie.

00:14:38.200 --> 00:14:39.310
Listen.

00:14:39.310 --> 00:14:43.200
Her race will attack anyone that tries to deceive them

00:14:43.200 --> 00:14:46.670
when their brains pick up even the faintest sound of a lie.

00:14:47.310 --> 00:14:52.880
Which means that us standing here, safe and sound, is proof that we aren't lying one bit!

00:14:55.460 --> 00:14:56.140
Now...

00:14:56.680 --> 00:14:59.930
Let's finish up your work, and return to your home planet!

00:14:59.930 --> 00:15:02.140
Everyone's waiting for your return.

00:15:07.720 --> 00:15:08.980
Hey...

00:15:09.700 --> 00:15:10.810
You're going?

00:15:11.520 --> 00:15:13.680
But... They aren't lying.

00:15:15.660 --> 00:15:18.430
I want to go home... back to everyone...

00:15:36.010 --> 00:15:36.660
Akagawa!

00:15:36.660 --> 00:15:38.140
What the hell do you think you're doing?

00:15:38.350 --> 00:15:39.950
They're obviously lying!

00:15:39.950 --> 00:15:40.510
But...

00:15:40.780 --> 00:15:43.440
It doesn't matter if your tongue doesn't react!

00:15:43.440 --> 00:15:45.000
You can just tell by looking at them!

00:15:45.000 --> 00:15:48.460
Do you seriously think they look like they're telling you the truth?!

00:15:49.760 --> 00:15:50.660
Akagawa.

00:15:51.640 --> 00:15:52.800
You're damn right!

00:15:53.380 --> 00:15:53.780
Wait!

00:16:03.700 --> 00:16:04.880
Tch. Damn brats.

00:16:06.620 --> 00:16:09.470
Don't underestimate us adults!

00:16:16.540 --> 00:16:19.160
I see! So that's what you really look like!

00:16:19.160 --> 00:16:20.490
You guys wouldn't sell at all.

00:16:26.950 --> 00:16:27.640
Shimizu!

00:16:29.620 --> 00:16:30.170
Yokota!

00:16:59.550 --> 00:17:00.590
Giga Bomb!

00:17:15.160 --> 00:17:15.940
Okay.

00:17:20.790 --> 00:17:21.620
Battle Light!

00:17:29.210 --> 00:17:30.650
Let's go, Yokota!

00:17:30.650 --> 00:17:31.770
Yeah, Shimizu!

00:18:04.080 --> 00:18:05.120
I've figured it out.

00:18:06.660 --> 00:18:09.250
They were modifying their voices with these.

00:18:10.120 --> 00:18:12.800
That's why you couldn't detect their lies.

00:18:14.060 --> 00:18:15.800
What happened to the other four?

00:18:15.800 --> 00:18:16.710
They're safe, right?

00:18:18.760 --> 00:18:19.800
Answer me!

00:18:21.490 --> 00:18:22.610
Tell her.

00:18:22.610 --> 00:18:24.260
If you don't, I'll kill you.

00:18:24.260 --> 00:18:25.750
Wait a second!

00:18:25.750 --> 00:18:27.100
I'll tell her, okay?

00:18:33.520 --> 00:18:35.190
We sold them all...

00:18:35.620 --> 00:18:36.730
Probably...

00:18:37.340 --> 00:18:40.220
No, they're definitely... all dead.

00:19:04.860 --> 00:19:07.410
All I have is myself now...

00:19:10.980 --> 00:19:13.590
I'm... all alone...

00:19:27.390 --> 00:19:29.020
You're not alone.

00:19:37.080 --> 00:19:38.710
I'm Shimizu Yoshiki!

00:19:40.540 --> 00:19:41.960
Momochi Osamu.

00:19:43.620 --> 00:19:45.090
Yokota Kunimitsu.

00:19:46.740 --> 00:19:47.720
Mayuzumi Mayo.

00:19:49.420 --> 00:19:50.760
Akagawa Taiyo!

00:19:53.120 --> 00:19:54.720
You can count on us!

00:20:01.670 --> 00:20:03.190
Thank you for everything.

00:20:04.220 --> 00:20:06.630
This is my cell phone number.

00:20:06.630 --> 00:20:09.080
Call me anytime. I'll pick right up.

00:20:09.080 --> 00:20:11.310
Watch what you say, man! You're gonna get stabbed.

00:20:26.200 --> 00:20:27.220
Until next time.

00:20:32.470 --> 00:20:34.480
I'll call!

00:20:47.720 --> 00:20:49.160
Yokota...

00:20:50.490 --> 00:20:53.240
I don't wanna go to America!

00:20:53.240 --> 00:20:55.130
Finally, he says what he feels.

00:20:55.130 --> 00:20:56.820
What should I do, man?!

00:20:56.820 --> 00:20:57.870
How should I know?

00:21:05.840 --> 00:21:06.920
Come on.

00:21:13.360 --> 00:21:14.670
Don't cry.

00:21:16.290 --> 00:21:17.970
I'm not crying!

00:21:20.110 --> 00:21:21.180
Hello?

00:21:21.180 --> 00:21:22.860
Yes, I saw the news.

00:21:23.650 --> 00:21:24.400
Yeah.

00:21:24.770 --> 00:21:28.400
One of the two heads of our company was killed by someone.

00:21:29.020 --> 00:21:32.280
Right, right... The asshole one.

00:21:32.280 --> 00:21:36.030
So we're going to go through some unprecedented personnel changes.

00:21:36.030 --> 00:21:37.620
The employees going overseas are all going to be reconsidered...

00:21:37.970 --> 00:21:39.980
You mean I have to unpack everything?

00:21:39.980 --> 00:21:42.360
I'll do it when I get home.

00:21:42.700 --> 00:21:46.040
Anyway, hurry up and tell Yoshiki.

00:22:01.410 --> 00:22:05.030
Oh, lovely! Your tail is split!

00:22:26.630 --> 00:22:27.270
Are you ready?

00:22:27.660 --> 00:22:38.170
Do not fear 'The Now' searching for something that can't be seen across this infinite distance

00:22:38.170 --> 00:22:52.390
Under the hundred million glittering lights, I found you searching for your dream

00:22:52.390 --> 00:23:01.150
An infinite world filled with glass shards

00:23:02.320 --> 00:23:13.210
Growing up I felt I knew many meaningless things

00:23:13.210 --> 00:23:20.670
Shining like a jewel, you soar in the sky, no past, no future

00:23:20.670 --> 00:23:26.010
The answer is beyond the sky

00:23:26.010 --> 00:23:36.520
Do not fear 'The Dream', in a distant
place where truth and lies are unseen

00:23:36.520 --> 00:23:52.250
Under the hundred million glittering lights, flowers sway in the wind

00:23:56.030 --> 00:23:56.740
Kisaragi High's Baseball Club

